            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Tampa to Orlando covers roughly 77 miles (124 km) across Central Florida, linking the Gulf Coast's largest city with the theme park capital of the world. Although this isn't a high-speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak's Floridian train offers a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a drive - especially when factoring in I-4's notorious traffic congestion and construction delays.</p>

