            <h2>What This Means for Travelers</h2>
            <p>Taking the train between Tampa and Orlando gives you a short, laid-back travel experience. It's comparable to driving time but lets you relax, use Wi-Fi, stretch your legs, and enjoy views of Florida's interior, including citrus groves, lakes, and small towns. Compared to road travel, the train avoids freeway traffic stress (especially on the perpetually congested I-4) and delivers you straight into Orlando without needing a car.</p>

            Key Points:
            <ul>
                <li>Perfect for day trips or weekend getaways to theme parks, though the single daily departure limits flexibility.</li>
                <li>Traveling by train allows you to work, read, or simply enjoy the scenery along Florida's diverse landscapes.</li>
                <li>Consistent daily schedules ensure predictable travel planning, though with only one daily option, timing is crucial.</li>
                <li>The short duration makes this route ideal for those who want a stress-free alternative to I-4 driving without the hassle of airport security.</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Train Duration by Type</h2>
