            <ul>
                <li><b>Coach: </b>Perfect for a budget-friendly option without sacrificing comfort. Seats are spacious with generous legroom, and the café car is accessible to all passengers. For the short 1.5-hour journey, Coach is the practical choice for most travelers.</li>
                <li><b>Sleeper Accommodations:</b> Better for those seeking privacy, a bed, and included meals - though for the short Tampa-Orlando segment, Sleeper rooms are generally not cost-effective. They are more commonly booked by passengers traveling the full Chicago-Miami route.</li>
